Q: Text horizontally next to an image on a navbar A: <p>Ah, yeah very common issue when navigating the various HTML elements! Your <strong>Headings</strong> are going to be block elements by default so they will always push themselves onto a new line by default.</p>
<p>Since I see you're already using <em>Bootstrap</em>, I suggest you just add a couple of utility classes directly on your <code>&lt;a&gt;</code> tag and no additional CSS is needed.</p>
<pre class="lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;nav class=&quot;navbar navbar-expand-lg bg-transparent&quot;&gt;
  &lt;div class=&quot;container-fluid justify-content-center&quot;&gt;

    &lt;a class=&quot;navbar-brand m-3 d-flex align-items-center&quot; href=&quot;#&quot;&gt;
      &lt;img src=&quot;../images/main/unssaf_marquee.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;marq&quot; width=&quot;150&quot; height=&quot;225&quot; class=&quot;me-3&quot;&gt;

      &lt;h1 class=&quot;style2 mb-0&quot;&gt;
        &lt;strong&gt;WELCOME TO Parker Bradley &lt;br&gt;Community FOUNDATION&lt;/strong&gt;
      &lt;/h1&gt;
    &lt;/a&gt; 

  &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/nav&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>Here's a direct link to the docs for reference: <a href="https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.3/utilities/flex/" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.3/utilities/flex/</a></p>

Q: how to have generic constrained type A: <p>Perhaps you could use <a href="http://www.scala-lang.org/api/current/index.html#scala.PartialFunction" rel="nofollow">partial functions</a>?</p>

<pre><code>val strOf10: PartialFunction[String, String] = { case str if (str.length == 10) =&gt; str};

val a = List("a", "abc", "abcdefghij");

scala&gt; a collect strOf10
res5: List[String] = List(abcdefghij)
</code></pre>
